<div id="pg-help" class="pg" aria-label="Find Stillbirth and Baby Loss Support by Country">
  <div class="pg-inner">
    <div class="crisis"><p>If you are in crisis right now, <strong>please reach out</strong> to your country's emergency services or a mental health line. You are not alone.</p></div>
    <span class="sec-eye">Global Resources</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">Find Support in <em>Your Country</em></h2>
    <p class="sec-body" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">Select your country to see verified charities, helplines, hospital bereavement teams, and funeral support resources.</p>
    <div class="cg" id="csel2"></div>
    <div class="cr" id="cres2">
      <h3 class="cr-title" id="cr-t2"></h3>
      <p class="cr-sub" id="cr-s2"></p>
      <div class="rg" id="cr-cards2"></div>
      <div id="cr-funeral2" style="display:none">
        <p class="fsec-title">&#x1F54A; Funeral Arrangements &amp; Memorial Support</p>
        <div class="rg" id="cr-fcards2"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="lt-content" style="display:none"><div class="lt-custom">
<h3 class="lt-h">Legal definition of stillbirth in Lithuania</h3>
<p><strong>Stillbirth</strong> &mdash; a baby born who died from 22 weeks of pregnancy through to the due date.</p>
<p><strong>Registration threshold</strong> &mdash; since 1991, stillbirths must be registered from 500g weight or 22 weeks gestation.</p>
<p><strong>Stillbirth rate</strong> &mdash; 2.6 per 1,000 total births (2021).</p>
<h3 class="lt-h">What happens to babies after late miscarriage or stillbirth</h3>
<span class="lt-lead">Late miscarriage (before 22 weeks)</span>
<ul>
<li>No birth or death certificate is issued.</li>
<li>No legal requirement for burial or cremation.</li>
<li>The hospital may offer a collective burial or cremation (several babies together).</li>
<li>Parents can choose to arrange a burial or cremation themselves.</li>
</ul>
<span class="lt-lead">Stillbirth (22 weeks and over)</span>
<ul>
<li>A medical death notice is issued by a doctor &mdash; used for funeral arrangements.</li>
<li>A birth or death certificate is not issued for stillbirths (only a medical death notice).</li>
<li>There is no separate stillbirth certificate (unlike the UK system, where one is issued).</li>
<li>Parents may request an autopsy (this requires consent).</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="lt-h">Aftercare for mothers in Lithuanian hospitals (2024&ndash;2025)</h3>
<p><strong>Postpartum depression assessment</strong> &mdash; as of 1 July 2024, family doctors must assess emotional well-being using the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS).</p>
<p><strong>State-funded care</strong> &mdash; medical assistance during pregnancy, birth, and the post-natal period is fully financed by the State.</p>
<h3 class="lt-h">Seeing and holding your baby</h3>
<p>In Lithuania, it is less common for parents to see or hold their baby after stillbirth or pregnancy loss. Many families are not encouraged to do this, and some hospitals may not offer it as a standard option. This is different from practices in countries like the Netherlands, the UK, or Australia, where seeing and holding the baby is considered part of compassionate, supportive care.</p>
<p>MIMATIS wants to support you in knowing that this choice is available to you. If you wish to see or hold your baby, you can request this from your healthcare team. You are not obligated to do so, but many parents later say that having this time with their baby helped them in their grief and gave them a moment to truly meet their child before saying goodbye.</p>
<p>Whatever you choose, your decision is valid. There is no &ldquo;right&rdquo; way to respond to this loss.</p>
<p>Hospital protocols vary. Some hospitals may be more flexible about time with your baby, while others may have stricter policies. If you feel your wishes are not being respected, you can:</p>
<ul>
<li>Ask to speak with the <strong>hospital social worker</strong>.</li>
<li>Request to speak with the <strong>department director</strong> or <strong>patient rights representative</strong>.</li>
<li>Contact a <strong>support organisation</strong> (such as Angel Mothers or the Crisis Pregnancy Center) for guidance.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="lt-h">Creating memories</h3>
<p>In Lithuania, hospitals may not routinely offer memory-making options. Some hospitals might not suggest:</p>
<ul>
<li>Taking photos of your baby.</li>
<li>Creating hand or foot prints.</li>
<li>Keeping mementos (hair, clothes, bracelet).</li>
</ul>
<span class="lt-lead">You have the right to</span>
<ul>
<li>Keep mementos (clothes, blanket, bracelet, ultrasound).</li>
<li>Have time with your baby to create memories.</li>
</ul>
<p>Whatever you choose is valid. There is no &ldquo;right&rdquo; way to remember your baby.</p>
<h3 class="lt-table-title">Organisations</h3><div class="lt-table-wrap"><table class="lt-table"><thead><tr><th>Organisation</th><th>Services</th><th>Contact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Angel Mothers (Angelų mamos)</td><td>Support for mothers who lost a baby — miscarriage, ectopic, premature, stillbirth.</td><td><a href="tel:060667323">Tel: 0 606 67323</a><br><a href="https://www.angelumamos.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">angelumamos.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Education &amp; Counselling Centre</td><td>Psychosocial support for families who lost a baby.</td><td><a href="tel:0860759340">Tel: 0 860 759340</a><br><a href="https://www.kudikionetektis.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kudikionetektis.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Crisis Pregnancy Center (Krizinio nėštumo centras)</td><td>Support for miscarriage, premature loss, pregnancy termination, and postpartum depression.</td><td><a href="tel:060357912">Tel: 0 603 57912</a><br><a href="https://krizinionestumocentras.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">krizinionestumocentras.lt</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="lt-table-title">Support helplines</h3><div class="lt-table-wrap"><table class="lt-table"><thead><tr><th>Helpline</th><th>Contact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hope Line &mdash; emotional support, 24/7</td><td><a href="tel:116123">Tel: 116 123</a><br><a href="https://www.viltieslinija.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">viltieslinija.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Women&rsquo;s Support Line &mdash; 24/7</td><td><a href="tel:080066366">Tel: 0 800 66366</a><br><a href="https://www.pagalbosmoterimslinija.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pagalbosmoterimslinija.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Don&rsquo;t Be Alone &mdash; support line for men</td><td><a href="tel:060411119">Tel: 0 604 11119</a><br><a href="https://www.nelikvienas.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nelikvienas.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Crisis Response Team &mdash; emergency support</td><td><a href="tel:1815">Tel: 1815</a><br><a href="https://www.kriziukomanda.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kriziukomanda.lt</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="lt-table-title">Funeral services</h3><div class="lt-table-wrap"><table class="lt-table"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Contact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ATERNA</td><td><a href="tel:065229506">Tel: 0 652 29506</a><br><a href="https://www.aterna.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aterna.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>GRAUDUVA</td><td><a href="tel:068656806">Tel: 0 686 56806</a><br><a href="https://www.grauduva.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">grauduva.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>K2 LT CREMATORIUM</td><td><a href="tel:063397722">Tel: 0 633 97722</a><br><a href="https://www.lietuvoskrematoriumas.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lietuvoskrematoriumas.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>LAKRIMA</td><td><a href="tel:052725044">Tel: 0 527 25044</a><br><a href="https://www.lakrima.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lakrima.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>RIMTIS</td><td><a href="tel:037346666">Tel: 0 373 46666</a><br><a href="https://www.rimtis.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rimtis.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>VILNIUS FUNERAL PALACE RITUALAS</td><td><a href="tel:052154690">Tel: 0 521 54690</a><br><a href="https://www.vlr.lt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vlr.lt</a></td></tr><tr><td>PRARADIMAS, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37065068220">Tel: 370 650 68220</a></td></tr><tr><td>AMŽINA RAMYBĖ, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37034966048">Tel: 370 349 66048</a></td></tr><tr><td>AKMEKA, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37068393951">Tel: 370 683 93951</a></td></tr><tr><td>AMŽIAUS VARTAI, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37060348802">Tel: 370 603 48802</a></td></tr><tr><td>AMŽINASIS AUKURAS, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37065041148">Tel: 370 650 41148</a></td></tr><tr><td>GEDULO RŪMAI, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37065141019">Tel: 370 651 41019</a></td></tr><tr><td>LAIDOJIMO PASLAUGŲ CENTRAS, UAB</td><td><a href="tel:+37068222883">Tel: 370 682 22883</a></td></tr><tr><td>AMŽINYBĖS NAMAI</td><td><a href="tel:+37065966666">Tel: 370 659 66666</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══ GARDEN ═══ -->
<div id="pg-garden" class="pg" aria-label="Memorial Garden - Plant a flower in your baby's name">
  <div class="pg-inner">
    <span class="sec-eye">In Memoriam</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">The Memorial <em>Garden</em></h2>
    <p class="sec-body">Plant a flower in your baby's name &mdash; it will bloom here alongside others, a testament to each precious, irreplaceable life.</p>
    <p class="fc" id="fc" style="margin-top:1.75rem">&#127800;&thinsp; Loading flowers...</p>
    <div class="gsky" id="gc">
      <div class="gstar" style="width:3px;height:3px;left:12%;top:12%;--d:2.4s"></div>
      <div class="gstar" style="width:2px;height:2px;left:28%;top:7%;--d:3.1s"></div>
      <div class="gstar" style="width:3px;height:3px;left:47%;top:16%;--d:2.2s"></div>
      <div class="gstar" style="width:2px;height:2px;left:65%;top:9%;--d:3.8s"></div>
      <div class="gstar" style="width:4px;height:4px;left:81%;top:14%;--d:2.7s"></div>
      <div class="gstar" style="width:2px;height:2px;left:55%;top:4%;--d:3.3s"></div>
      <div class="gnd2"></div><div class="gnd"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pfa">
      <div class="pf"><label>Baby's name</label><input type="text" id="bname" placeholder="e.g. Sofia" maxlength="20"></div>
      <div class="pf"><label>Choose a flower</label>
        <select id="ftype">
          <option value="&#x1F338;">&#x1F338; Cherry Blossom</option>
          <option value="&#x1F337;">&#x1F337; Tulip</option>
          <option value="&#x1F33C;">&#x1F33C; Daisy</option>
          <option value="&#x1F33A;">&#x1F33A; Hibiscus</option>
          <option value="&#x1F490;">&#x1F490; Bouquet</option>
          <option value="&#x1F33B;">&#x1F33B; Sunflower</option>
          <option value="&#x1F339;">&#x1F339; Rose</option>
          <option value="&#x1FAB7;">&#x1FAB7; Lotus</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="pf"><label>Year</label><input type="number" id="byear" placeholder="2023" min="1900" max="2026"></div>
      <button class="pf-btn" id="plant-btn">Plant</button>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:.67rem;color:var(--ghost);margin-top:.85rem;text-align:center">Anonymous. No data stored beyond this session.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══ RESEARCH ═══ -->
<div id="pg-research" class="pg" aria-label="Stillbirth and Pregnancy Loss Research Library">
  <div class="pg-inner">
    <span class="sec-eye">Evidence &amp; Knowledge</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">Research <em>Library</em></h2>
    <p class="sec-body" style="margin-bottom:2.75rem">Curated academic studies on miscarriage, stillbirth, neonatal death, prevention, and grief &mdash; including European research. Click any study to read the full paper.</p>
    <div class="frow">
      <button class="fbtn active" data-filt="all">All Studies</button>
      <button class="fbtn" data-filt="sb">Stillbirth</button>
      <button class="fbtn" data-filt="nn">Neonatal Death</button>
      <button class="fbtn" data-filt="mc">Miscarriage</button>
      <button class="fbtn" data-filt="pr">Prevention</button>
      <button class="fbtn" data-filt="gr">Grief &amp; Mental Health</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slist" id="slist"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══ GUIDANCE ═══ -->


<!-- ═══ INFO CARDS ═══ -->


<!-- ═══ BOOKS ═══ -->
<div id="pg-books" class="pg">
  <div class="pg-inner">
    <span class="sec-eye">Recommended Reading &amp; Memorial Art</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">Books &amp; <em>Remembrance</em></h2>
    <p class="sec-body" style="margin-bottom:3rem">When a baby has died, it can be helpful and comforting to read books written by others who have walked the same path. Literature on loss offers recognition, understanding, and the quiet reassurance that you are not alone in your experience. Below you will find a careful selection of books, as well as a memorial art service. The loss of a baby is also deeply felt by siblings and other young children in the family. Books written for children can help them give voice to their grief and find meaning in the loss together.</p>
    <div class="resources-grid">
      <div class="res-card">
        <span class="res-type">Book &middot; Memoir</span>
        <div class="res-title">Still Here: A Memoir of Love, Loss, and Triumph After Stillbirth</div>
        <div class="res-author">Alishia Anderson</div>
        <p class="res-desc">A personal testimony of how love, faith, and support can bring you back from the abyss after the loss of a precious baby. Alishia lost her first-born son DJ at 28 weeks and wrote this book to remove the shield of shame and isolated suffering around baby loss &mdash; while also giving voice to the often-forgotten perspective of a grieving father.</p>
        <a class="res-link" href="https://www.amazon.com/Still-Here-Memoir-Triumph-Stillbirth/dp/1732582505?&linkCode=sl1&tag=up010-20&linkId=15276ce384d15fb44e27d47ce53e871e&language=en_US" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy on Amazon</a>
      </div>
      <div class="res-card">
        <span class="res-type">Book &middot; Children's</span>
        <div class="res-title">Happy Tears &amp; Rainbow Babies</div>
        <div class="res-author">Natasha Carlow</div>
        <p class="res-desc">A beautifully illustrated children's book for ages 4&ndash;8 that gently opens the conversation about miscarriage and rainbow babies. A loving, age-appropriate way for families to share the tender conversation about pregnancy loss with young children &mdash; written from a mother to her children, for families everywhere.</p>
        <a class="res-link" href="https://www.amazon.com/Happy-Rainbow-Babies-Natasha-Carlow/dp/1948604205?ie=UTF8&linkCode=sl1&tag=up010-20&linkId=036c1bbfc02bc6280f913b4c28ec4818&language=en_US" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy on Amazon</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="artist-card">
      <div>
        <p class="artist-eye">Memorial Art &middot; Commission a piece</p>
        <h3 class="artist-title">A hand-drawn portrait of your baby's <em>name.</em></h3>
        <p class="artist-desc">Viktorija Liau is a digital artist who creates beautiful, personalised hand-drawn name illustrations as a memorial keepsake. Each piece is unique &mdash; a gentle, lasting way to honour your baby and keep their name alive.</p>
        <a class="res-link" href="https://viktorijaliau.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="margin-top:1.25rem;display:inline-block">Visit Viktorija's studio</a>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align:center">
        <div style="width:110px;height:110px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--green-light);border:2px solid var(--green);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:2.2rem;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);margin:0 auto">V</div>
        <p style="font-size:.68rem;color:var(--soft);margin-top:.7rem">viktorijaliau.net</p>
      </div>
