  <!-- LETTERS SUBVIEW -->
  <div class="gs-sub-view" id="gss-letters">
    <div class="gs-inner-nav">
      <button class="gs-back" id="gs-back-letters">Back</button>
      <span class="gs-bc-sep">/</span>
      <span class="gs-bc-cur">Finding the right words</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gs-inner-body">
      <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--soft);line-height:1.85;max-width:520px;margin-bottom:2.25rem;border-left:2px solid var(--bdr);padding-left:1rem;font-style:italic">In moments of profound loss, words can feel impossible to find. These templates are here so you do not have to start from nothing. Take what feels right, change what does not, and make it your own.</p>
      <div id="gs-acc-list"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT TO SAY SUBVIEW -->
  <div class="gs-sub-view" id="gss-words">
    <div class="gs-inner-nav">
      <button class="gs-back" id="gs-back-words">Back</button>
      <span class="gs-bc-sep">/</span>
      <span class="gs-bc-cur">What to say</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gs-inner-body">
      <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--soft);line-height:1.85;max-width:520px;margin-bottom:2.25rem;border-left:2px solid var(--bdr);padding-left:1rem;font-style:italic">When someone you love loses a baby, it can be hard to know what to say. You don&rsquo;t need the perfect words &mdash; you just need to show up. This page will help you do that with care.</p>
      <div class="gs-say-lbl"><span class="gs-say-dot" style="background:#C77FE0"></span><span style="color:#993556;font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase">Please avoid saying these</span></div>
      <h3 class="gs-say-sec-title">Things that can cause pain, even when well-meant</h3>
      <div class="gs-say-cards" id="gs-no-say"></div>
      <div class="gs-say-lbl"><span class="gs-say-dot" style="background:#0097B2"></span><span style="color:#00708A;font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase">These words tend to help</span></div>
      <h3 class="gs-say-sec-title">What to say instead</h3>
      <div class="gs-say-cards" id="gs-yes-say"></div>
      <div style="background:var(--off);border:0.5px solid var(--bdr);padding:1.75rem;margin-top:.5rem">
        <span style="font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);display:block;margin-bottom:.65rem">The most important thing</span>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:400;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:.75rem">How to simply be present</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--mid);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1.25rem">Sometimes there are no right words. What matters most is that you showed up, remembered, and didn&rsquo;t disappear. Grief can be very lonely. Your presence matters more than your words.</p>
        <div class="gs-pres-grid">
          <div class="gs-pres-card"><span class="gs-pres-lbl">Say their baby&rsquo;s name</span><p class="gs-pres-txt">Using the baby&rsquo;s name &mdash; if shared &mdash; is one of the most meaningful things you can do.</p></div>
          <div class="gs-pres-card"><span class="gs-pres-lbl">Check in weeks later</span><p class="gs-pres-txt">A message one month or six months later means more than you know. Most people disappear after week one.</p></div>
          <div class="gs-pres-card"><span class="gs-pres-lbl">Offer something specific</span><p class="gs-pres-txt">&ldquo;I&rsquo;m bringing dinner Thursday&rdquo; is far more helpful than &ldquo;let me know if you need anything.&rdquo;</p></div>
          <div class="gs-pres-card"><span class="gs-pres-lbl">Remember key dates</span><p class="gs-pres-txt">The due date, the anniversary. A simple &ldquo;thinking of you today&rdquo; is deeply meaningful.</
      <!-- MISSION COMPACT -->
      <div class="who-compact">
        <div class="who-compact-card">
          <span class="who-compact-label">Mission</span>
          <p class="who-compact-text">To ensure every bereaved parent &mdash; wherever they live, whatever language they speak &mdash; can find support after the loss of a baby. Without barriers. Without cost.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="who-compact-card">
          <span class="who-compact-label">Vision</span>
          <p class="who-compact-text">A world where bereavement care is not a privilege of language or geography, but a right that follows every family, wherever life has taken them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="who-compact-card">
          <span class="who-compact-label">Why we exist</span>
          <p class="who-compact-text">Support after loss exists &mdash; but scattered, hard to find, and almost always in one language. MIMATIS brings everything into one place, at any hour, in any country.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- TEAM -->
      <h2 class="who-team-heading">The people behind <em>MIMATIS</em></h2>

      <div class="who-member">
        <div class="who-photo" style="background:var(--green-light);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:1.8rem;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);width:80px;height:80px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--green-light);flex-shrink:0">V</div>
        <div>
          <div class="who-name">Victoria</div>
          <span class="who-role">Founder</span>
          <span class="who-loc">Europe</span>
          <p class="who-bio">Mother of three, with more than ten years of experience in sales and client relationships. Victoria lost her daughter Maya at 34 weeks in the Netherlands in 2022. MIMATIS was born from that loss &mdash; and from the realisation that the support she needed simply did not exist in the form families need it most.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      

      

      

